<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Tenmu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 631–686</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Tenmu (c. 631–686) was the 40th emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, reigning from 673 to 686. A younger brother of Emperor Tenji, he won the throne in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jinshin-war">Jinshin War</a> of 672. He strengthened royal power over the aristocracy, ordered the compilation of a law code and national histories, and is often regarded as the first ruler to use the title tennō (emperor).</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-tenmu.jpg" alt="Emperor Tenmu" width="320" height="445" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Xwdgtpwga · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%A4%A9%E6%AD%A6%E5%A4%A9%E7%9A%87%E5%BE%A1%E5%BD%B1%E3%80%81%E9%87%91%E5%89%9B%E5%B1%B1%E5%AF%BA%E6%89%80%E8%94%B5.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
